  "sourceNotes": [
    "Attempt SIX QUESTIONS from eight is whole-examination selection. Retain every task in all eight questions; do not create duplicate examination bundles.",
    "Q7(c)(ii): one of three diagrams is the correct answer, and all three must be assessed. This is a single identification-and-reasoning task, not a choose-one practice route.",
    "One root four times the other is a condition on roots, not a choice. Both values are required.",
    "Hence, or otherwise permits another solution method, not a finite selection. All required roots, values, proof steps and derivatives are retained. Alternative published methods remain inside their task.",
    "Mathematical errors or omissions: −3. Numerical slips: −1. Misreadings: −1 provided the task is not oversimplified.",
    "A correct relevant step earns its attempt mark; deductions cannot reduce it below that floor. No mark strictly between zero and the attempt mark.",
    "Worthless work: zero. Hit or miss: full marks or zero.",
    "Best of two or more attempts accepted unless indicated otherwise; same error in same section penalised once.",
    "Particular cases, unrequested verifications/diagrams, and serious blunders/omissions/misreadings earn attempt marks at most.",
    "Detailed task-specific exceptions and caps must remain beside all official worked alternatives.",
    "Q3(c)(ii) asks for a conjugated matrix and hence its power. Keep the linked calculation together, with its two separate five-mark controls and the condition that the first matrix be diagonal before the second award is available.",
    "Q7(b)(i) requires both parametric derivatives in one printed task. Both independent ten-mark components remain visible and separately scoreable; the subsequent derivative-ratio task is separate.",
    "Setup, simplification and completion allocations are steps of one response, not separate questions.",
    "Q6(c)(ii) is 5 marks, attempt 2 in both the summary and detailed allocation. A later note refers to “2nd 5 marks”; this discrepancy is explained without creating extra marks.",
    "Historical matrices are retained in algebra; original matrix notation, proofs, integrals, graphs and alternative solutions remain visible.",
    "Shared marking-note blocks are labelled; only deductions relevant to the named task apply."
